      "raw_text": "South-Southwest of Southwestern Mexico (EP99):\nPersistent but disorganized shower and thunderstorm activity is \nassociated with a broad area of low pressure well south-southwest \nof the southwestern coast of Mexico. Environmental conditions are \nconducive for development, and a tropical depression is expected to \nform over the next couple of days as the system moves generally \nnorthward off the coast of southwestern Mexico. Interests along the \nsouthwestern and west-central coast of Mexico should monitor the \nprogress of this system.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...high...80 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...high...90 percent.",
